  "data": {
    "accession": "PXD057110",
    "title": "Finding the LC3-interactors in senescent human A549 cells during influenza A virus infection",
    "additionalAttributes": [],
    "projectDescription": "To screen age-related regulators of mitophagy, we examined LC3-interacting proteins by proximity-dependent biotin identification. LC3B was cloned into a mammalian expression vector tagged with a mitochondrial OMM-targeted APEX2 (mito-APEX) label for proximity-based identification of LC3-interacting proteins localized or trafficked to mitochondria during influenza virus infection. Senescent A549 cells, transfected with the mito-APEX-tagged LC3 plasmid for 18 hours, revealed mitochondrial localization of LC3. Following 18 hpi and biotin affinity capture, biotinylated proteins were purified and analyzed by mass spectrometry to identify LC3-interacting proteins.",
    "sampleProcessingProtocol": "Cell samples were collected and lysed in 1 ml of Western and IP lysis buffer containing protease and phosphatase inhibitors. A portion of each whole cell lysate sample was kept to ascertain protein expression levels, and 500 μg of cell lysate was used for the IP assays. Lysates were incubated with Streptavidin(SAV) MagBeads for 8 h at 4 °C under gentle rotation. The beads were then washed four times with cold lysis buffer and analysed by LC/MS.",
    "dataProcessingProtocol": "Analysing the cellular localization of protein via GeneCards website.",
